    "result_text": "Green. Both findings addressed \u2014 I agree with both; they're exactly the single-source-of-truth idiom the codebase enforces.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 split format contract (agreed).** Introduced `OwnerCustomerCode`, a single-source-of-truth helper mirroring `OwnerIdentity`/`OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerLocality`. It owns both sides of the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format:\n- `of(Owner)` constructs the code.\n- `regionOf(String)` parses the `REGION` half back out.\n- `regionFor(Owner)` + the `UNKNOWN_REGION` constant absorb the previously-duplicated null-region\u2192`\"UNKNOWN\"` mapping.\n\n`AssignCustomerCode` now just calls `OwnerCustomerCode.of(owner)`, and `OwnerMapper.locality` calls `regionOf(...)` with a `regionFor(owner)` fallback \u2014 so the separator/layout knowledge lives in exactly one place.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 duplicated telephone fallback (agreed).** Moved the \"canonical E.164, or raw value when it can't form one, or empty for null\" policy into `OwnerTelephone.toE164OrRaw(...)`, next to the rule it builds on. Both `OwnerIdentity.key` and `OwnerCustomerCode.of` now call it; the private copy in `OwnerIdentity` is gone.\n\n**Tests:** full suite **BUILD SUCCESS** (1/1, 0 failures). Acceptance behaviour (`customerCode` matching `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and all values derived from it) is unchanged.",
